                <dia:string>#StructHandle is used for registering a struct or a class.
What we want in registering a struct is member variables
and getter and setter methods. Other methods can't be 
registered. There may be some event callback methods with
specific signature that can be bound and called when an 
event happens. All types of member variables of struct must
be registered. These variables and getter and setter and 
event callback are all we need to access from rml files.#</dia:string>
