        <dia:object type="UML - Note" version="0" id="O323">
          <dia:attribute name="obj_pos">
            <dia:point val="105,-90"/>
          </dia:attribute>
          <dia:attribute name="obj_bb">
            <dia:rectangle val="104.95,-90.05;148.19,-70.65"/>
          </dia:attribute>
          <dia:attribute name="meta">
            <dia:composite type="dict"/>
          </dia:attribute>
          <dia:attribute name="elem_corner">
            <dia:point val="105,-90"/>
          </dia:attribute>
          <dia:attribute name="elem_width">
            <dia:real val="43.139999999999993"/>
          </dia:attribute>
          <dia:attribute name="elem_height">
            <dia:real val="19.300000000000004"/>
          </dia:attribute>
          <dia:attribute name="text">
            <dia:composite type="text">
              <dia:attribute name="string">
                <dia:string>#There are four kind of views: 
* DataViewCommon: This is used for views inside a element tag. &lt;input data-visible="variable_one &gt; variable_two"&gt;
* DataViewText: This is used for views inside text area of tags. This type of views always are inside {{}}. &lt;input&gt;{{title}}&lt;/input&gt;
* DataViewAlias: This is used for views used with templates. Using data-alias-[variable_name] as attribute of outter element of
  a template we can change the value of [variable-name] data view inside the template. 
  &lt;template name="temp"&gt;
    &lt;head&gt;&lt;/head&gt;
      &lt;body&gt;
	&lt;div data-attr-icon="icon"&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;h1&gt;{{ title }}&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;/body&gt;
  &lt;/template&gt;
  This template can then be used with different variables as follows:
  &lt;div data-alias-icon="other_icon" data-alias-icon="other_title"&gt;
    &lt;template src="data-title"/&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  Now the {{title}} of template changes to value of {{other_title}} and icon changes to other_icon.
* DataViewFor: Repeats the element and its children n times for each item in the data variable which must be a data array type.
  &lt;p data-for="subject, i : subjects"&gt;{{i + ': ' + subject}}&lt;/p&gt;
  This paragraph element will be repeated for number of array size of subjects. If the size of subjects is three, it becomes:
  &lt;p&gt;{{i + ': ' + subject}}&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;{{i + ': ' + subject}}&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;{{i + ': ' + subject}}&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p style="display: none;"/&gt;#</dia:string>
              </dia:attribute>
              <dia:attribute name="font">
                <dia:font family="monospace" style="0" name="Courier"/>
              </dia:attribute>
              <dia:attribute name="height">
                <dia:real val="0.80000000000000004"/>
